mdx#with-cattery-modules","17":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/quick-start.mdx#default-template","18":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/quick-start.mdx#after-initialization","19":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/quick-start.mdx#registry-shortcuts","20":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/templates.mdx#available-templates","21":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/templates.mdx#all-templates","22":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/templates.mdx#usage-examples","23":"/home/runner/work/nixcafe-docs/nixcafe-docs/apps/develop-templates/src/pages/templates.mdx#how-templates-work"},"fieldIds":{"category":0,"subtitle":1,"text":2,"title":3,"titles":4},"fieldLength":{"0":[0,0,19,1,0],"1":[0,0,32,2,1],"2":[0,0,7,4,1],"3":[0,0,67,5,1],"4":[0,0,13,3,6],"5":[0,0,30,4,6],"6":[0,0,37,2,1],"7":[0,0,26,2,1],"8":[0,0,14,2,0],"9":[0,0,35,2,2],"10":[0,0,96,2,2],"11":[0,0,50,4,2],"12":[0,0,70,1,2],"13":[0,0,10,2,0],"14":[0,0,10,4,2],"15":[0,0,18,3,2],"16":[0,0,20,3,2],"17":[0,0,25,2,2],"18":[0,0,25,2,2],"19":[0,0,24,2,2],"20":[0,0,112,2,0],"21":[0,0,112,2,2],"22":[0,0,37,2,2],"23":[0,0,61,3,2]},"averageFieldLength":[0,0,39.583333333333336,2.5416666666666665,1.7916666666666667],"storedFields":{"0":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#contributing","subtitle":"","text":" This project follows GitHub Flow. All contributions must be made via pull requests against the main branch.","title":"Contributing","titles":[],"type":"page"},"1":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#development-shell","subtitle":"","text":" git clone https://github.com/nixcafe/develop-templates.git\ncd develop-templates\nnix develop The dev shell provides nixfmt, deadnix, and statix with git-hooks enabled. Formatting and linting run automatically on every commit. Run checks manually: nix flake check","title":"Development Shell","titles":["Contributing"],"type":"section"},"2":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#creating-a-feature-branch","subtitle":"","text":" git checkout -b feat/my-new-template","title":"Creating a Feature Branch","titles":["Contributing"],"type":"section"},"3":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#adding-a-new-nix-template","subtitle":"","text":" Create a repository under nixcafe-develop with your template files (a standard flake.nix + flake.lock + any project files)Add the repository as a flake input in flake.nix: templates-<name> = {\n  url = \"github:nixcafe-develop/<repo-name>\";\n  flake = false;\n}; Create templates/<name>/default.nix: { inputs, ... }:\n{\n  description = \"Description of your template\";\n  path = \"${inputs.templates-<name>}\";\n  welcomeText = ''\n    # Template Name — Nix Development Environment\n    Run `nix develop` to enter the dev shell.\n  '';\n} Run checks: nix flake check Open a pull request to the main branch.","title":"Adding a New Nix Template","titles":["Contributing"],"type":"section"},"4":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#on-pull-request","subtitle":"","text":" Git hooks checks (nixfmt, deadnix, statix) run automatically on all PRs.","title":"On Pull Request","titles":["Contributing","CI/CD (GitHub Actions)"],"type":"section"},"5":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#on-push-to-main","subtitle":"","text":" The Nix flake is automatically published to FlakeHub as nixcafe/develop-templates with rolling versioning. This ensures flakes consuming these templates are not affected by GitHub API rate limits.","title":"On Push to Main","titles":["Contributing","CI/CD (GitHub Actions)"],"type":"section"},"6":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#branch-protection","subtitle":"","text":" The main branch is protected: Pull request reviews are required (at least 1 approval)Status checks must pass before mergingStale reviews are dismissed when new commits are pushed All development happens on feature branches and is merged to main via pull requests.","title":"Branch Protection","titles":["Contributing"],"type":"section"},"7":{"category":"","href":"/contributing#code-style","subtitle":"","text":" Nix: follow nixfmt outputNo unused bindings (deadnix)statix lint warnings must be clean{ ... }: empty patterns should use _: instead (except where the spread is intentional)","title":"Code Style","titles":["Contributing"],"type":"section"},"8":{"category":"","href":"/#develop-templates","subtitle":"","text":" Curated Nix flake project templates — bootstrap reproducible development environments with a single command.","title":"develop-templates","titles":[],"type":"page"},"9":{"category":"","href":"/#quick-start","subtitle":"","text":" # Register the alias (once)\nnix registry add beans \"github:nixcafe/develop-templates\"\n\n# Bootstrap a project\nnix flake init -t beans#node\nnix flake init -t beans#python\nnix flake init -t beans#rust\n\n# Enter the dev shell\nnix develop That's it — no Docker, no manual toolchain setup, no version managers.","title":"Quick Start","titles":["develop-templates"],"type":"section"},"10":{"category":"","href":"/#available-templates","subtitle":"","text":" TemplateStackWhat's includednix (default)Nixnixfmt, deadnix, statix — Nix dev shell with formatting & lintingnodeNode.js / Bun / DenoNode.js, Bun, Deno, nipythonPythonPython auto-configured, ruff, hatchlingrustRustcargo, rustc, clippy, rustfmt, rust-analyzerjavaJavaGraalVM JDK, Maven, GradlekotlinKotlinGraalVM JDK, Kotlin compiler, GradlelatexLaTeXLaTeX with Nix formatterstypstTypstTypst with Nix formattersnix-configNixOS / macOSNixOS, nix-darwin, home-managercolmena-configNixOS + ColmenaNixOS with Colmena deploymentsecretsSecretsagenix/ragenix with YubiKeypurrpurr Frameworkpurr project (mkFlake)purr-flake-partspurr + flake-partspurr with flake-parts See the Available Templates page for descriptions and usage examples for every template.","title":"Available Templates","titles":["develop-templates"],"type":"section"},"11":{"category":"","href":"/#why-nix-flake-templates","subtitle":"","text":" Reproducible — identical environments across Linux, macOS, and WSLNo Docker overhead — native Nix builds, no container runtimeDeclarative — tools, dependencies, and env vars in one flake.nixZero-install bootstrap — nix flake init -t + nix developPolyglot — one toolchain for all programming languagesCI-friendly — same environment locally and in CI","title":"Why Nix Flake Templates?","titles":["develop-templates"],"type":"section"},"12":{"category":"","href":"/#architecture","subtitle":"","text":" Each template is a thin wrapper pulling content from a dedicated repository under nixcafe-develop: # templates/node/default.nix\n{ inputs, ... }:\n{\n  description = \"Node.js development environment\";\n  path = \"${inputs.templates-node}\";\n  welcomeText = ''\n    # Node.js — Nix Development Environment\n    Run `nix develop` to enter the dev shell.\n  '';\n} The template flake itself is built with purr — directory convention, auto-discovery, zero boilerplate. See the Quick Start page for detailed setup instructions, and Contributing to add your own template.","title":"Architecture","titles":["develop-templates"],"type":"section"},"13":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#quick-start","subtitle":"","text":" nix flake init -t \"github:nixcafe/develop-templates#${template_name}\" --refresh","title":"Quick Start","titles":[],"type":"page"},"14":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#nix-flake-init-direct","subtitle":"","text":" nix flake init -t \"github:nixcafe/develop-templates#${template_name}\" --refresh","title":"nix flake init (direct)","titles":["Quick Start"],"type":"section"},"15":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#nix-registry-recommended","subtitle":"","text":" Add to your Nix registry for shorter commands: nix registry add beans \"github:nixcafe/develop-templates\"\nnix flake init -t beans#${template_name}","title":"nix registry (recommended)","titles":["Quick Start"],"type":"section"},"16":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#with-cattery-modules","subtitle":"","text":" If you use cattery-modules for NixOS deployment, the templates are pre-registered: nix flake init -t beans#${template_name}","title":"With Cattery Modules","titles":["Quick Start"],"type":"section"},"17":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#default-template","subtitle":"","text":" The default template is nix — a Nix development shell with formatting, linting, and dead code detection tools. Used when no template is specified: nix flake init -t beans","title":"Default Template","titles":["Quick Start"],"type":"section"},"18":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#after-initialization","subtitle":"","text":" nix develop    # Enter the development shell The nix develop command drops you into a fully provisioned dev environment with all tools, dependencies, and pre-commit hooks configured.","title":"After Initialization","titles":["Quick Start"],"type":"section"},"19":{"category":"","href":"/quick-start#registry-shortcuts","subtitle":"","text":" We recommend registering the alias once: nix registry add beans \"github:nixcafe/develop-templates\" This allows shorter commands: nix flake init -t beans#rust\nnix flake init -t beans#python\nnix flake init -t beans#node","title":"Registry Shortcuts","titles":["Quick Start"],"type":"section"},"20":{"category":"","href":"/templates#available-templates","subtitle":"","text":" TemplateLanguage / Use CaseDescriptionnixNixNix development environment with nixfmt, deadnix, and statix (default template)nodeNode.js / JavaScript / TypeScriptNode.js development environment with Node.js, Bun, Deno, and nipythonPythonPython development environment with auto-configured Python version, ruff, and hatchlingrustRustRust development environment with cargo, rustc, clippy, rustfmt, and rust-analyzer source resolutionjavaJava / JVMJava development environment with GraalVM JDK, Maven, and GradlekotlinKotlin / JVMKotlin development environment with GraalVM JDK, Kotlin compiler, and GradlelatexLaTeXLaTeX document authoring environment with Nix formatters and pre-commit hookstypstTypstTypst document authoring environment with Nix formatters and pre-commit hooksnix-configNixOS / macOSNixOS, nix-darwin, and home-manager configuration with auto-discovered systemscolmena-configNixOS DeploymentNixOS Configuration with Colmena deployment and ISO/image buildssecretsSecrets ManagementEncrypted secrets management with agenix/ragenix and YubiKey supportpurrpurr Frameworkpurr project template using mkFlake (standalone)purr-flake-partspurr + flake-partspurr project template with flake-parts integration","title":"Available Templates","titles":[],"type":"page"},"21":{"category":"","href":"/templates#all-templates","subtitle":"","text":" TemplateLanguage / Use CaseDescriptionnixNixNix development environment with nixfmt, deadnix, and statix (default template)nodeNode.js / JavaScript / TypeScriptNode.js development environment with Node.js, Bun, Deno, and nipythonPythonPython development environment with auto-configured Python version, ruff, and hatchlingrustRustRust development environment with cargo, rustc, clippy, rustfmt, and rust-analyzer source resolutionjavaJava / JVMJava development environment with GraalVM JDK, Maven, and GradlekotlinKotlin / JVMKotlin development environment with GraalVM JDK, Kotlin compiler, and GradlelatexLaTeXLaTeX document authoring environment with Nix formatters and pre-commit hookstypstTypstTypst document authoring environment with Nix formatters and pre-commit hooksnix-configNixOS / macOSNixOS, nix-darwin, and home-manager configuration with auto-discovered systemscolmena-configNixOS DeploymentNixOS Configuration with Colmena deployment and ISO/image buildssecretsSecrets ManagementEncrypted secrets management with agenix/ragenix and YubiKey supportpurrpurr Frameworkpurr project template using mkFlake (standalone)purr-flake-partspurr + flake-partspurr project template with flake-parts integration","title":"All Templates","titles":["Available Templates"],"type":"section"},"22":{"category":"","href":"/templates#usage-examples","subtitle":"","text":" # Node.js\nnix flake init -t beans#node\n\n# Python\nnix flake init -t beans#python\n\n# Rust\nnix flake init -t beans#rust\n\n# Java\nnix flake init -t beans#java\n\n# Kotlin\nnix flake init -t beans#kotlin\n\n# LaTeX\nnix flake init -t beans#latex\n\n# Typst\nnix flake init -t beans#typst\n\n# Nix dev\nnix flake init -t beans#nix\n\n# NixOS config\nnix flake init -t beans#nix-config\n\n# Colmena config\nnix flake init -t beans#colmena-config\n\n# Secrets\nnix flake init -t beans#secrets\n\n# purr project\nnix flake init -t beans#purr\n\n# purr + flake-parts\nnix flake init -t beans#purr-flake-parts","title":"Usage Examples","titles":["Available Templates"],"type":"section"},"23":{"category":"","href":"/templates#how-templates-work","subtitle":"","text":" Each template is defined as a thin default.nix wrapper: # templates/node/default.nix\n{ inputs, ... }:\n{\n  description = \"Node.js development environment\";\n  path = \"${inputs.templates-node}\";\n  welcomeText = ''\n    # Node.js — Nix Development Environment\n    Run `nix develop` to enter the dev shell.\n  '';\n} The template content lives in a separate repository under nixcafe-develop and is pulled in as a flake input (flake = false). This keeps the templates flake lightweight while allowing each template to evolve independently.","title":"How Templates Work","titles":["Available Templates"],"type":"section"}},"dirtCount":0,"index":[["zero",{"2":{"11":1,"12":1}}],["keeps",{"2":{"23":1}}],["key",{"2":{"20":1,"21":1}}],["keypurrpurr",{"2":{"10":1}}],["kotlin",{"2":{"10":2,"20":3,"21":3,"22":1}}],["you",{"2":{"16":1,"18":1}}],["your",{"2":{"3":2,"12":1,"15":1}}],["yubikey",{"2":{"20":1,"21":1}}],["yubikeypurrpurr",{"2":{"10":1}}],["yubi",{"2":{"10":1,"20":1,"21":1}}],["x",{"2":{"10":2,"20":2,"21":2,"22":1}}],["gradlelatex",{"2":{"1